  "query_preview": "..\nToday Through Monday...\n\nUpper ridging with repeated shortwaves out of the southwest will \nbe the main pattern this week. Hot to very hot temperatures \ncontinue today, with an Extreme Heat Warning in effect until \nmidnight tonight for Custer, Powder River, Fallon, and Carter \nCounties. Look for high temperatures across the area in the upper\n80s to 100F (warmest in the east).\n\nThe focus continues to transition towards a warm and moist setup \ninto the weekend, as deep moisture continues to stream into the \nregion from the southwest. Exceptionally high precipitable water \nvalues are shown by models and ensembles. This will result in the \nthreat for heavy to very heavy rainfall with showers and \nthunderstorms the next couple days. \n\nToday will be similar to Tuesday, with slow-moving afternoon \nshowers and storms lasting into the overnight hours. The threat \nfor strong to severe thunderstorms is low though, with weaker \ninstability and minimal shear. The threat for excessive rainfall \nexists once again, with another Marginal Risk including and west \nof a Sheridan County to Musselshell County line. A Flash Flood \nWatch has been issued for these areas from Noon MDT today to 3 AM\nMDT Thursday. The most likely timing based on the most recent Hi-\nRes runs is 2 PM MDT today to 12 AM MDT Thursday.\n\nModels continue to show a stationary front developing near the \nDakotas border through Wednesday evening. This looks to keep \nsoutheasterly and dry flow into southern Montana. Relative \nhumidity values will be in the teens to low 20s percent. Winds do \nnot look to be that strong so the need for fire weather highlights\nis low, though the risk for grass fires will be elevated.\n\nAnomalous moisture and unsettled flow continues through the \nweekend, with daily chances for afternoon/evening showers and \nthunderstorms across the western and central areas. Look for high \ntemperatures in the 80s and 90s through the weekend.\n\nMatos/Archer",
